{{en-verb|discipl}}

# {{lb|en|religion|transitive}} To convert (a person) into a disciple.
# {{lb|en|religion|transitive}} To [[train]], [[educate]], [[teach]].
#* '''1590''', Edmund Spenser, ''The Faerie Queene'', IV.i:
#*: fraile youth is oft to follie led, / Through false allurement of that pleasing baite, / That better were in vertues '''discipled''' {{...}}
## {{lb|en|Christianity|certain|_|denominations}} To [[routine#Adjective|routine]]ly [[counsel]] (one's [[peer#Etymology 2|peer]] or [[junior#Noun|junior]]) [[one-on-one]] in their discipleship of Christ, as a fellow [[affirm]]ed disciple.

